//! generator and run `cargo run -p geom-gen -- write`. CI runs `cargo run -p geom-gen -- check` and
//! fails on any difference.
//!
//! The exact paths of the generated predicates in the plain-`i128` variant: each step in `i128`, or
//! in its certificate's wide type when it does not fit 127 bits, with both operands widened to that
//! type and the general `checked_mul`, so no product is narrower than its result's type. On
//! WebAssembly every product then goes through `__multi3`, the library routine Rust's `i128`
//! multiply becomes there (chapter 23.3 of the kernel architecture,
//! `projects/engines/geometry/architecture/23-performance.md`; piece G42). For each predicate,
//! `<predicate>_value` performs the steps of the predicate module's `value`, in their order and
//! with their names, each held in the type above, so it returns the same value, as an `i128` where
//! the shipped path returns an `i64`. The benchmarks compare the two on every target, and the tests
//! check that they agree on every input they draw and at the grid's extremes.
//!
//! Guarantees: as each predicate module's `value`. Every step is a checked method, the certificate
//! in the predicate module's header bounds every step within the type it is held in here (a type at
//! least as wide as the one the certificate names), so a step never returns `None` for an input in
//! the domain; nothing depends on overflow checks being on. geom-gen's independent checker
//! re-derives every line from its own derivation.
//!
//! Method: each predicate's steps as its module's certificate derives them, held as chapter 23.3
//! describes the baseline of its comparison of exact-path variants,
//! `projects/engines/geometry/architecture/23-performance.md`.
//!
//! Cost: the predicate module's `value`, with each product at the width of its result.

